From Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: DryhoppedIPA <DryhoppedIPA@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 8 Aug 2026 04:53:11 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] radv,ac: GFX1013 compute queue fix (identity, exposure,
 ACE dispatch WA)

Three changes that together make the GFX1013 (BC-250) dedicated compute
queues usable:

- Expose the ACE compute queue family unconditionally.  Upstream hides it
  because stock kernels have a broken compute-queue lifecycle; this driver
  requires the V33 kernel patches from this repository, which repair it.
- Route GFX1013 through the existing Iceland/Tonga async-compute
  threadgroup workaround (thread-dimension dispatch mode).  The part
  mis-executes threadgroup-dimension dispatches with PARTIAL_TG_EN in a
  state it cold-boots into, corrupting every RADV meta transfer on the
  ACE queues.  Verified: dEQP-VK.synchronization2.* 7034 fail -> 7034
  pass with the workaround, 0 regressions.

Note: The GFX10.1 IP minor version correction (ASICREV_IS GFX1013 for
ver_minor = 1) is already upstream in Mesa 26.2.1 via !43465 and does
not need to be re-applied.

Do not ship the Mesa half without the kernel half.
---
 src/amd/common/ac_gpu_info.c | 10 ++---
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/amd/common/ac_gpu_info.c b/src/amd/common/ac_gpu_info.c
--- a/src/amd/common/ac_gpu_info.c
+++ b/src/amd/common/ac_gpu_info.c
@@ -483,10 +483,8 @@
        */
       info->ip[ip_type].num_queues = 1;
    } else if (ip_info->available_rings) {
-      /* GFX1013 is known to have broken compute queue */
-      if (ip_type == AMD_IP_COMPUTE && device_info->family == FAMILY_NV &&
-          ASICREV_IS(device_info->external_rev, GFX1013))
-         return false;
+      /* GFX1013: the compute queue is exposed unconditionally.  This driver
+       * must run only on a kernel carrying the V33 compute-queue lifecycle
+       * repair; on stock GFX1013 kernels the queue must stay closed.
+       */
 
       info->ip[ip_type].num_queues = util_bitcount(ip_info->available_rings);
@@ -1019,7 +1017,8 @@
     * dimension mode.
     */
    info->has_async_compute_threadgroup_bug = info->family == CHIP_ICELAND ||
-                                             info->family == CHIP_TONGA;
+                                             info->family == CHIP_TONGA ||
+                                             info->family == CHIP_GFX1013;
 
    /* GFX7 CP requires 32 bytes alignment for the indirect buffer arguments on
     * the compute queue.
